# /etc/systemd/system/search-services.slice on cloudlayer (#6852): the reader-facing search services, kept OUT of
# sourcelibrary.slice, where the Claude jobs run. On 2026-10-17 l7a's vector service hung for ~15 min because it
# shared that slice with the jobs: an sl-tsc pushed the slice over MemoryHigh and the kernel throttled every
# process in it, the service included. A request path must not depend on what a job is type-checking.
#
# Members: keyword-search.service (Slice= in its unit) and caddy.service (caddy-search-slice.conf drop-in).
# MemoryMin reserves the hot index set from reclaim. Phase 2 measured ~2 GB of the memory-mapped index charged to
# the unit after a parity run, plus ~80 MB of process; 4G leaves room for it to grow under shadow, then serve,
# traffic. cgroup v2 protection is hierarchical: a unit's MemoryMin counts only up to its parent's, so it is set
# here AND on the unit AND on search.slice, the parent the dash in this name implies (without it, all three are 0). MemoryMax 10G matches the unit's own cap, so the box's worst case for Source Library is
# 14G (jobs) + 10G (search) of 31 GB, and the Cloud Layer globe (system.slice) keeps the rest.
[Unit]
Description=Source Library search services (keyword page service + its TLS front), outside the jobs slice

[Slice]
MemoryMin=4G
MemoryHigh=9G
MemoryMax=10G
CPUWeight=50
IOWeight=50
TasksMax=2000
